et me re-examine.\n\nClue 1: Wang and Zhao are taller than the Engineer. So, Engineer is the shortest. So, Engineer must be either Wang or Zhao, but clue 2 says Secretary is shorter than Wang. So, if Engineer were Wang, then Secretary would have to be shorter than Wang, but Engineer is Wang, so that would mean Secretary is shorter than Engineer, which contradicts clue 1 because Engineer is the shortest. Therefore, Engineer cannot be Wang. So, Engineer must be Zhao.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought Engineer can't be Zhao because of clue 3. Let me check again.\n\nIf Engineer is Zhao, then from clue 1: Zhao < Wang and Zhao < Zhang. From clue 2: Secretary < Wang. From clue 3: Zhang ≠ Secretary in height. So, if Engineer is Zhao, then Secretary must be either Wang or Zhang. But clue 2 says Secretary < Wang, so Secretary can't be Wang because that would mean Secretary is Wang, but clue 2 says Secretary is shorter than Wang, so Secretary must be someone else. Wait, no, clue 2 says Secretary is shorter than Wang, so Secretary can be either Wang or Zhao, but if Engineer is Zhao, then Secretary can't be Zhao because Engineer is Zhao. So, Secretary must be Wang? But clue 2 says Secretary is shorter than Wang, so if Secretary is Wang, that would mean Wang is shorter than himself, which is impossible. Therefore, Engineer can't be Zhao either.\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me try a different approach.\n\nLet's list the possible roles and see who can be where.\n\nRoles: Director, Secretary, Engineer.\n\nPeople: Zhang, Wang, Zhao.\n\nClues:\n\n1. Engineer is shorter than Wang and Zhao.\n\n2. Secretary is shorter than Wang.\n\n3. Zhang and Secretary are not the same height.\n\nFrom clue 1: Engineer is the shortest.\n\nFrom clue 2: Secretary is shorter than Wang, so Secretary < Wang.\n\nFrom clue 3: Zhang ≠ Secretary in height, so if Secretary is someone, Zhang is taller or shorter, but not the same.\n\nSince Engineer is the shortest, and Secretary is shorter than Wang, let's see.\n\