st important. So, this option is probably incorrect.\n\nOption D: The virtue, ability, diligence, performance, and honest of civil servants are equally important. The context says that all these aspects are assessed, but it emphasizes performance. It doesn\'t say they are equally important. So, this option is probably incorrect because it\'s not stated that all are equally important.\n\nGoing back to Option A, the context does say that performance is emphasized, which could imply that it\'s the most important, but it\'s not explicitly stated. However, the other options don\'t seem to fit as well. Option B is too absolute, and Options C and D are incorrect based on the context. So, I think Option A is the best choice, even though the wording is a bit tricky.\n']
