ause of taxes, so if taxes are abolished, they might become competitive. So, they would continue serving unless taxes are abolished. Wait, that seems a bit circular. If taxes are abolished, they would be competitive, so they would continue. So the statement in D is saying they won't continue unless taxes are abolished, which is the opposite. So D might not be correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.\n"]
