n all three.\n\nThat leaves M or P as the one serving on all three sub-committees.\n\nLet\'s try M as the one serving on all three. So, M is in sub-committees 1, 2, and 3.\n\nNow, since M is in all three, we need to assign the other members, making sure that H and I are not in the same sub-committee. So, H and I must be in different sub-committees.\n\nAlso, F and G cannot be in the same sub-committee.\n\nLet me try to assign the members.\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nWait, but in this case, F is in sub-committees 1 and 3, G is in 2 and 3, H is in 1, I is in 2.\n\nBut wait, F and G are both in sub-committee 3, which violates the condition that F and G cannot be in the same sub-committee. So, that\'s not allowed.\n\nLet me try another arrangement.\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nAgain, F and G are in sub-committee 3, which is not allowed.\n\nHmm, maybe I need to adjust.\n\nLet me try:\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nBut again, F and G are together in sub-committee 3.\n\nAlternatively, maybe:\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nNo, same problem.\n\nWait, perhaps M is in all three, but F and G are in different sub-committees.\n\nLet me try:\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nBut again, F and G are together in sub-committee 3.\n\nWait, maybe I need to have F and G in different sub-committees altogether.\n\nLet me try:\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nNo, same issue.\n\nWait, perhaps I\'m approaching this wrong. Maybe M is in all three, but F and G are in different sub-committees, and H and I are in different sub-committees.\n\nLet me try:\n\nSub-committee 1: M, F, H\n\nSub-committee 2: M, G, I\n\nSub-committee 3: M, F, G\n\nBut again, F and G are togeth