t be necessary.\n\nWait, but let me think again. The argument says the butterfly is active only at night, so the discovery must have been at night. But what if the scientists could detect it during the day? Then the conclusion wouldn't hold. So the assumption is that the scientists couldn't detect it during the day, which is option B.\n\nSo the answer should be B.\n</think>\n\nThe argument depends on the assumption that the scientists couldn't detect the butterfly during the day. This is because if they could, the conclusion that they found it at night wouldn't necessarily be true.\n\nAnswer: B",
