['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nWhile the number of cod in the North Atlantic has greatly decreased, the number of seals has increased from 1.5 million to about 2.5 million. Some people think that seals are responsible for the reduction of cod, but seals rarely feed on cod, so it is impossible that a large increase in the number of seals has led to a significant decline in the number of cod.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, would most strongly weakens the above argument ?\n# Options:\nA) In the traditional fishing belt of the cod, a large number of seals cause great inconvenience to fishing vessels.\nB) Pollution from the sea does more damage to cod than to seals.\nC) Before the increase in the number of seals, the number of cod in the north atlantic decreased greatly.\nD) Cod eat almost only hairy scale fish, which are also the main food for seals.']
