["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nDepartment manager: I'd like to replace the M-type computers in my department with V-type computers. General manager: Why? Department manager: The cost of training new employees to operate V-shaped computers can be reduced by 20%. General manager: But that's not a good enough reason. We can simply hire only those who already know how to use M-type computers.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, will most seriously weaken the general manager's opposition to replacing M-type computers with V-computers?\n# Options:\nA) At present, all employees of the company are required to participate in learning how to use m-type computers with new functions\nB) Once employees have learned how to use computers, they are more likely to change jobs than before\nC) Employees who are proficient in using m-type computers will demand higher income than those who are expected to have no experience in using computers\nD) The average productivity of employees in the general manager's company is lower than that of its competitors"]
