er is C) My country's dependence on imported crude oil has increased.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - The country's economic policies are expected to slow growth, reducing demand for oil and natural gas.\n   - Oil production is increasing (175 million tons, up 1%).\n   - Consumption is rising (over 300 million tons, up 12%).\n   - Imports are also increasing (over 100 million tons, up 30%).\n\n2. **Analyzing Each Option:**\n   - **A)** Incorrect. Production is increasing, so supply isn't tight.\n   - **B)** Not directly supported. The text doesn't specify that consumption is mainly from imports.\n   - **C)** Correct. Imports are increasing, indicating more dependence on them.\n   - **D)** Incorrect. Consumption and demand are increasing, not decreasing.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The only valid inference is that the country's dependence on imported oil has increased.\n\n**Answer:** C",
