['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nSome studies claim that cancer cells are afraid of heat, and high body temperature can fight cancer. The most cancer-prone organs of the human body, including the lungs, stomach, large intestine, breast, etc., are all parts of the body with low body temperature, and high temperature organs such as the heart are not easy to get cancer. Therefore, you can  raise your body temperature to fight cancer by doing exercise, drinking hot water, bathing and other ways.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, can best refute the above assertion?\n# Options:\nA) Affected by breathing, diet, etc., the temperature of the human mouth is generally lower than that of the rectum, but the incidence of rectal cancer worldwide is higher than that of oral cancer.\nB) The human body temperature has a precise regulation mechanism, which is basically stable, and there is no obvious temperature difference between the various organs in the body.\nC) Hyperthermia may help radiotherapy or some chemotherapy to play a better role, but research data to prove its reliability is still insufficient.\nD) Malignant tumors rarely occur in the heart because the cardiomyocytes here no longer divide or proliferate, regardless of the temperature.']
