tion. This doesn't relate to the discussion at all. The context is about the mass of the universe and antimatter, not about using antimatter for exploration. So C is irrelevant.\n\nD) Scientists have discovered antimatter in the laboratory, and it is now possible to produce some antimatter in the laboratory. The context doesn't mention anything about laboratory discoveries or production of antimatter. It talks about findings in the universe, not in labs. So D is not relevant.\n\nSo the only relevant premise is B, assuming that Einstein's calculations are correct because they led to the conclusion about the mass being zero, which in turn affects the belief in the existence of antimatter.\n</think>\n\nThe premise assumed in the discussion is that Einstein's calculations through the theory of relativity are correct.\n\nAnswer: B",
