tely different from developed countries. The context doesn't provide any information about the external environment during industrialization and modernization. It only talks about the per capita GNP range and the resulting social shocks. So I don't think D is supported by the given context.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the correct answer should be C because it directly relates to the period of social shock described in the context.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is C) Many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks in the process of their modernization.\n\n**Answer:** C",
