['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nObligatory alternative action refers to a situation in which the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is an optional act of obligation?\n# Options:\nA) When a was driving normally, a pedestrian named wang rushed to a from the sidewalk and wang was injured\nB) B drunk driving, pedestrian wang also drunk, from the sidewalk suddenly rushed to b, wang was injured\nC) C driving speeding, pedestrian wang across the road, c too late to brake, wang hit\nD) D overload driving, pedestrian wang across the road, fortunately, ding emergency brake, did not hit wang']
