ould mean the half-life is longer, thus refuting the scientist's point.\n\nSo the correct answer is C.\n\nWait, but I'm a bit confused because I thought the scientist's point was based on the specific finding, so if environmental factors can change the decay rate, that would mean the half-life isn't fixed, so maybe the scientist's conclusion is too hasty. So C would show that the half-life isn't as short as the scientist thinks, thus making it possible to reconstruct DNA, thus refuting the scientist's point.\n\nYes, I think C is the correct answer.\n"] 18%|█▊        | 111/600 [1:31:25<14:03:14, 103.46s/it]
