["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nWhy are the brain sizes of some primates larger than other animals? The reason is usually considered to be social behavior, that is, primates live in larger and more complex social groups. In order to better handle various social relationships, they Need a bigger brain.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if which of the following is true, the above point of view can't be questioned?\n# Options:\nA) It is easier to predict the size of the brain through the dietary characteristics of primates rather than the complexity of the community\nB) Some primates such as orangutans usually live alone, but their brains are also large\nC) The size of the cerebral cortex is not directly related to the size of the brain, but it is very important for primate cognition, spatial reasoning ability, etc\nD) Among primates, fruit-eating animals have larger brains than leaf-eating animals. this is because fruits are more dispersed in time and space, and finding fruits is a more complicated task"]
