['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nHuman intelligence is not possible without human emotions. A computer is something that can never have emotions, so for that reason alone a computer will never be able to display intelligence.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?\n# Options:\nA) Someone or something is intelligent only if it can identify its emotions.\nB) Computer technology will not greatly advance beyond its current state.\nC) A computer could have emotions only if it could display intelligence.\nD) Being intelligent requires the capacity to have emotions.']
