['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nUnder the premise of honest research, it is very common to understand deviations or even errors in the analysis of specific experimental results, which is a normal process of scientific development. It can be said that there are varying degrees of misunderstandings or deviations in the analysis, conclusions and discussants of many academic papers, and the debate on this kind of academic issues is often one of the important driving forces of scientific development. The more cutting-edge scientific research, the more prone to misunderstanding and wrong conclusions.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the text intended to illustrate?\n# Options:\nA) The foundation of honest research is to respect the authenticity of the original experimental data\nB) It is understandable that scientific research based on honesty has made mistakes\nC) Experimental research should not draw conclusions lightly and should be verified repeatedly\nD) Inference and continuous revision of research conclusions are the driving force for scientific development']
