 normal and part of the process, which supports B. It also mentions that these discussions are a driving force, which supports D. However, the question is about what the text is illustrating, not necessarily the driving force.\n\nOption B directly addresses the common occurrence of mistakes in honest research, which is a key point in the context. Option D is more about the role of these debates as a driving force, which is also present but perhaps a bit more abstract.\n\nI think the main illustration is that it's understandable for research to have mistakes, so B is the best answer.\n</think>\n\nThe text illustrates that it's understandable for honest scientific research to have mistakes, as deviations and errors are normal parts of the process.\n\n**Answer: B**",
