['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nThe market as a way and means of resource allocation is not omnipotent and flawless. Market allocation is generally adjusted spontaneously by the invisible hand, that is, the law of value, the law of supply and demand and the law of competition. This kind of regulation brings lag, that is to say, there is a certain time delay from the signal feedback of price formation to the effect of product output.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, in this paragraph, which of the following options is the defect of market as a resource allocation?\n# Options:\nA) Spontaneity and competitiveness.\nB) Lag and adjustment.\nC) Lag and spontaneity.\nD) Competitiveness and adjustment.']
