["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIf home appliances going to the countryside gives home appliance enterprises the opportunity to open up the rural consumer market, then going to the city can better create better sales performance for enterprises. Because in cities, residents are more likely to accept new ways of life and consumption. If home appliances into the city also get the relevant policy support and subsidies of the government. Enterprises should have reason to explore new consumption potential in the urban market, so that urban low-income and unemployed residents can also benefit from the consumption of home appliances.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is conforming to the author's point of view?\n# Options:\nA) Home appliances go to the countryside, which may bring good sales performance to enterprises\nB) Urban low-income and unemployed residents need more policy support and subsidies\nC) The government should support enterprises'home appliances into the city and vigorously promote new products\nD) Compared with the rural market, the urban consumer market also has the potential to tap"]
