sion.\n\nOption D: In order to have a good marriage, we should have a correct view of marriage and attitude towards marriage. The passage discusses that money is still a factor, but it's not the only one. It also mentions that parents interfere based on family and educational backgrounds. So the conclusion here would be that having a correct view and attitude towards marriage is important, which aligns with D.\n\nWait, but the passage doesn't explicitly say that money is the only factor, just that it's still deeply rooted. So maybe the conclusion is more about the factors influencing marriage rather than the importance of affection or correcting views.\n\nI think D is the best answer because it's about having the right perspective and attitude, which the passage hints at by mentioning that even though love is free, parents still use other factors. So D seems to capture that idea.\n"]
