['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIt is generally believed that honesty is a matter of personal morality and has nothing to do with others, but personal morality is not only a personal problem, but it will also produce social effects through externalities-the debt that individuals get, Eventually, it may repay to the whole society. From the perspective of institutional economics, a good economic system and governance mechanism should be able to restrain negative externalities, otherwise the economic order may collapse. It is necessary to make the initiators bear their due responsibility through the system and mechanism, rather than letting others or the whole market pay for it.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most accurate summary of the main point of this passage?\n# Options:\nA) It is true that personal morality has to be paid for by the whole society\nB) The economic system is of great significance to the economic order\nC) Honesty is both a social issue and an economic issue\nD) System is needed to suppress negative externalities of dishonesty']
