['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nNational pricing: refers to the commodity prices and charging standards set by the government price department and the competent business department in accordance with the authority of the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is not subject to national pricing?\n# Options:\nA) A well-known shopping mall has newly imported a batch of high-end cashmere sweaters. for the credibility of the shopping mall, the boss decided to sell the new products at a 30% discount in the first three days of the market.\nB) On the eve of the start of school in the spring of 2005, the education bureau of a certain city issued a notice about the tuition and miscellaneous fees of various schools in the new semester, and asked the school to announce it.\nC) On the eve of the spring festival, in order to safeguard the interests of the general public and stabilize the order of the holiday market, the municipal price bureau approved and announced the maximum prices of some commodities such as poultry eggs, vegetables, and aquatic products.\nD) The charging standards for buses in nanjing are clearly: 1 yuan per ride for ordinary unmanned ticket vending vehicles, 2 yuan per ride for air-conditioned unmanned ticket vending vehicles, and 20% off for passengers with bus cards.']
