success id:  178
["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn order to implement the cultural strategy of strengthening the city, a city built two libraries in 2008 and 2010. At the end of 2008, a total of 70,000 citizens' library cards were issued, and a total of 130,000 citizens' library cards were issued by the end of 2010. In 2011, the city established a third library in the new district, which was completed and opened in early 2012. As of the end of 2012, the city had handled more than 200,000 library cards for citizens. The city government therefore believed that this measure was effective, because in just four years, the number of citizens coming into the libraries has nearly tripled.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the followings, if true, can weaken the above conclusion the most?\n# Options:\nA) The library need to constantly purchase new books, and the maintenance cost is also high, which will affect the construction of other cultural facilities in the city.\nB) There are two universities in the city, and many students have also applied for library cards for these three libraries.\nC) Many citizens who applied for the library card for the first library also applied for the library card for the other two libraries.\nD) The construction of the new district of the city was developing rapidly, and a large number of migrants have poured into the new district in 4 years."]
