er would be the one that's part of the formal curriculum. So the answer is either A, B, or C.\n\nWait, but the question is which is NOT an invisible curriculum. So the answer is the one that is part of the formal curriculum. So looking at the options, A is military training, which is part of the formal curriculum. So A is not invisible.\n\nBut wait, the question is asking which is NOT an invisible curriculum. So the answer is A, because it's part of the formal curriculum.\n\nWait, but I'm a bit confused because sometimes the interest in learning might be part of the formal curriculum as well. For example, if the teaching courses include training students to be interested in learning, that might be part of the formal curriculum.\n\nSo, to sum up, the answer is A because it's part of the formal curriculum, making it not invisible. The other options are either part of the formal curriculum or are extracurricular.\n"] 38%|███▊      | 227/600 [2:37:15<2:22:27, 22.91s/it]
