n't canvass the existing ones enough. If most previous donors donated without contact (C), that also suggests they didn't canvass them enough.\n\nBut the question is which provides more support. I think B is more about the composition of donors, implying that they didn't reach enough existing donors, which directly supports the argument. C is about the previous donors donating without contact, which might suggest that the university's fund-raisers didn't reach them, but it's a bit more indirect because it's possible that other fund-raisers did reach them.\n\nSo I think B is the better answer.\n"] 40%|████      | 241/600 [2:47:48<3:36:31, 36.19s/it]
