['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nA serious safety accident occurred in a coal mine. As for the cause of the accident, the four responsible persons A, B, C, and D have the following conclusions: A: If the direct cause of the accident is equipment failure, then someone must have violated the operating rules. B: It is true that someone has violated the operating rules, but the direct cause of the accident is not the equipment failure. C: The direct cause of the accident is indeed the equipment failure, but no one has violated the operation. D: The direct cause of the accident is the equipment failure.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if only one of the above determinations is true, which one of the following determinations is true?\n# Options:\nA) A is true, someone violated the rules of operation\nB) A is true, but no one violated the rules of operation\nC) B is true\nD) C is ture']
