at some professionals are age-biased, but the psychologist argues against this, so this is more of a premise rather than the main conclusion.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main conclusion is that elderly people should not be reluctant to undergo psychotherapy because they have advantages that make it beneficial for them.\n</think>\n\nThe main conclusion is that elderly people should not be reluctant to undergo psychotherapy because they have advantages that make it beneficial for them.\n\nAnswer: B",
