r people. The focus is more on encouraging them rather than comparing their benefits.\n\nD) Certain psychotherapists practice age discrimination.\nThe context mentions that some professionals are age-biased, but the psychologist argues against this, so this is more of a premise rather than the main conclusion.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main conclusion is that elderly people should not be reluctant to undergo psychotherapy because they have advantages that make it beneficial for them.\n"] 45%|████▌     | 271/600 [3:04:16<33:52,  6.18s/it]
