verwhelmed by something named "ranche." So B doesn\'t seem to fit.\n\nOption C refers to performance under a planned economy system. The context doesn\'t mention anything about a planned economy or how the market economy is performing. It\'s about the market price department setting maximum prices, which is more about regulation than performance under a specific economic system. So C doesn\'t seem relevant.\n\nOption D states that the price department has state pricing power. The context clearly mentions that the market price department announced maximum prices. This action implies that they have the authority to set these prices, which would come from state power. So D seems to be a direct conclusion from the context.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be D.\n']
