l Zhenyuan are ascetics. So, Guo Shu being an ascetic doesn\'t necessarily mean they\'re from Zhenyuan, but they could be. But the question is about whether Guo Shu is from Anxi or not.\n\nWait, maybe I\'m overcomplicating this. Let me think again. The context says all Anxi are vegetarians, and all Zhenyuan are ascetics. It doesn\'t say anything about the relationship between Anxi and Zhenyuan. So, Guo Shu being an ascetic doesn\'t tell us anything about their origin. Therefore, we can\'t infer anything about whether Guo Shu is from Anxi or not. So, option D also can\'t be inferred.\n\nWait, but that can\'t be right because the options must have one correct answer. Let me re-examine.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake. The context says all Zhenyuan are ascetics, but it doesn\'t say that all ascetics are Zhenyuan. So, Guo Shu is an ascetic, but we don\'t know if they\'re from Zhenyuan or another group. So, we can\'t say for sure that Guo Shu is not from Zhenyuan (option B) because maybe they are. But the question is about whether Guo Shu is from Anxi or not.\n\nWait, but the question is about whether Guo Shu is from Anxi or not. The context doesn\'t link Anxi and Zhenyuan in any way. So, Guo Shu could be from Anxi, but it\'s also possible they\'re from Zhenyuan or another group. Since the context doesn\'t specify, we can\'t infer anything about their origin relative to Anxi. So, options C and D are about Anxi, but without any information, we can\'t say for sure.\n\nWait, but the question is asking which can be inferred. So, perhaps none of the options can be inferred, but that\'s not possible because the options are A, B, C, D.\n\nWait, maybe I\'m missing something. Let me read the context again.\n\n"All Anxi people are vegetarians, while all Zhenyuan people are ascetics. Ascetics and vegetarians are like fire and water, and there is no conflict. Guo Shu is an ascetic."\n\nSo, the key points are:\n\n- Anxi → Vegetarian\n- Zhenyuan → Ascetic\n- Guo Shu is Ascetic\n\nNo