usion is that the increase in sales is because of the personalized products. So to support this, we need an option that shows that the personalized products are a significant driver of sales.\n\nOption A: If personalized sales were limited, it would contradict the manager\'s conclusion, so A is not supporting.\n\nOption B: If young people are trying new things, and they are a significant part of the customer base, then the personalized products would be more appealing to them, thus increasing sales. So B supports the manager\'s conclusion.\n\nOption C: Better display could lead to more sales overall, but not necessarily because of the personalized products. So C might support the overall sales increase but not specifically the personalized products.\n\nOption D: If both personalized and regular products were added, it\'s possible that the sales increase is due to both, which could mean that the personalized products are not the main reason. So D might not support the manager\'s conclusion as strongly.\n\nTherefore, the best option is B because it directly relates the popularity of the personalized products to the target demographic, which is likely contributing to the sales increase.\n']
