e operators taking the initiative. So this might not be the best fit.\n\nBetween A and B, both seem correct, but the question is about what the text is meant to emphasize. The text mentions relying on the masses and building a supervision network, which are both important. However, the main emphasis is on the public's role in supervision, so option B might be more central.\n\nWait, but option A is about building a supervision network, which is part of the process. Option B is about relying on the masses, which is the approach. The text says \"rely on the masses and mobilize the masses,\" so B seems more about the method, while A is about the tool. The question is about what the text emphasizes, so B might be the better answer.\n\nBut I'm a bit confused because both A and B are correct. Let me think again. The text says \"we should improve the reporting system of the masses, build a strict social supervision network,\" so building a supervision network is part of the solution. But the main point is that the masses should be relied upon, which is option B.\n\nSo, I think the answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe text emphasizes the role of the masses in supervising the network culture industry, highlighting their importance in resisting bad information. \n\nAnswer: B) The supervision of the network culture industry should rely on the strength of the masses.",
