['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nThe researchers asked children of different ages to use words to form semantic correspondence. For example, when children see the words eagle, bear and robin, they combine them best according to their meaning. The results showed that older participants were more likely to develop different types of false memory than younger participants. Because there are many forms of classification in their minds. For example, young children classify eagles and robins as birds, while older children classify eagles and bears as predators. Compared with children, they have a concept of predators in their minds.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following conforms to the context?\n# Options:\nA) Older children are more likely to have false memories than younger ones\nB) Older and younger children make different mistakes when remembering\nC) Children testify more reliably than teenagers or adults\nD) Depending on the nature of different events and the evidence and testimony, young children may sometimes remember more accurately']
