ferent events and the evidence and testimony, young children may sometimes remember more accurately." The context doesn\'t talk about accuracy in general or about evidence and testimony. It focuses on false memories, so this option isn\'t supported by the given information.\n\nSo, after evaluating each option, Option A directly matches the information provided in the context about older children having more false memories. The other options either don\'t address the issue or introduce unrelated concepts.\n']
