      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the answer to this logical reasoning question based on the given context. Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThe context is about Karl Polanyi and his statement regarding the market mechanism. He says that if the market is allowed to be the sole guide for the destiny of mankind, its natural environment, and the use of purchasing power, society will be destroyed. He talks about commodities and labor, stating that labor cannot be arbitrarily driven and used. Even if a person is abandoned, the system faces the unity of body, psychology, and morality under the title of person.\n\nSo, the question is asking for the gist of the statement. The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me break down the context. Polanyi is concerned about the market's role in society. He argues that when labor is commodified, the market doesn't just affect the economy but also the individual's identity and well-being. The market's unregulated use leads to issues because it doesn't consider the moral and psychological aspects of people.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) Unregulated markets will destroy society. This seems to align with Polanyi's point because he's worried about the market's sole guide leading to destruction.\n\nB) Labor is a special commodity. The context mentions that labor is a commodity, so this might be true, but is it the gist? The gist is more about the consequences of commodification.\n\nC) The unregulated market lacks moral attributes. This is a point made, but the main issue is more about how the market affects people beyond just economic factors.\n\nD) Labor cannot be commoditized. The context does say that labor cannot be arbitrarily driven, implying it can't be commodized without consequences, but the gist is more about the societal impact.\n\nSo, the main gist is about how unregulated markets lead to societal destruction because they don't consider the moral and psychological aspects of people. Therefore, 