e of the misunderstanding. Therefore, D is more about the cause, while B is about the evaluation itself.\n\nBut the question is asking what is discussed, not what the consequence is. The passage is explaining why the misunderstanding exists, so the cause is the main content. Therefore, the answer should be D.\n</think>\n\nThe passage discusses the historical misunderstanding about the evaluation of Chinese porcelain in Western history, specifically that tourists assume the evaluation is due to the official kiln, which is incorrect. Therefore, the main content is the cause of this misunderstanding.\n\nAnswer: D",
