aluation is due to the official kiln, but the author points out that this is incorrect. So the cause is discussed here.\n\nWait, so both B and D seem relevant. Let me think again. The question is about what is discussed. The passage is explaining the misunderstanding, so it's discussing the cause of the misunderstanding. Therefore, D is more about the cause, while B is about the evaluation itself.\n\nBut the question is asking what is discussed, not what the consequence is. The passage is explaining why the misunderstanding exists, so the cause is the main content. Therefore, the answer should be D.\n"]
