endence.\n\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation. External motivation would mean they rely on external factors, which is the opposite of field dependence. Field dependence is about being influenced by external, not dominating it.\n\nWait, but the question is asking which option belongs to field dependence. So, field dependence is about being influenced by external factors, especially social, and relying on external references. So, option B talks about having an opinion on others, which is influenced by others, an external factor. That fits.\n\nOption D is about being dominated by external motivation, which is more about how they act, not necessarily the processing of information. Field dependence is more about how information is processed, influenced by external factors.\n\nSo, the correct answer should be B.\n"]
