ng up the options. Option B says "Truth cannot be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed." That translates to "If truth is shut out, then all the doors of wrong are closed," which is Q → P. But the original is P → Q, so B is the converse, which isn\'t necessarily true. So B is not correct.\n\nSo the correct answer should be C.\n'] 80%|███████▉  | 478/600 [5:40:01<59:34, 29.30s/it]  
