ore about genetic modification, not hybridization. So C might be mixing up terms, and I think it\'s not the best answer.\n\nOption D: "A crop that transplants other life genes to produce additional characteristics." This is similar to C but uses "other life genes" which is a bit vague. The context specifies that the genes can come from any living organism, so D is a bit broad and not as precise as B. Also, it\'s more about the action (transplanting) rather than the result (additional genes).\n\nSo, putting it all together, the correct answer should be B because it directly refers to the additional genes that produce the extra traits, which is the main point of genetically modified crops as described in the context.\n']
