["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nUntil 1990, an oil exploration team in Mexico's Gocatan Peninsula stumbled upon a huge crater. Most of the crater is submerged at the bottom of the sea near the Yucatan Peninsula, with a width of about 160 to 240 kilometers. The age of the crater-covered sediment suggests that the giant crater was formed about 65 million years ago, coinciding with the extinction of the dinosaurs. The discovery of this evidence basically reached a consensus among scientists that the extinction of dinosaurs was caused by the impact of the meteorite on the earth.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the point that this paragraph is trying to make?\n# Options:\nA) Before 1990, no one would have thought that the extinction of dinosaurs was caused by meteorites hitting the earth\nB) The discovery of the crater made scientists more consistent with the cause of dinosaur extinction\nC) 65 million years ago, the area near the yucatan peninsula was dense with dinosaurs\nD) The crash of a meteorite is a natural phenomenon"]
