["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nGenuine happiness consists not in pleasurable feelings but instead in one' s sense of approval of one' s character and projects. Thus the happy life, in fact, tends to be the good life, where the good life is understood not -- as it usually is these days -- as a life of material well-being but rather as a morally virtuous life.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is an assumption required by the argument?\n# Options:\nA) A morally virtuous life requires the rejection of material well-being.\nB) People who approve of their own character and projects tend to lead morally virtuous lives.\nC) Attaining happiness is the real goal of people who strive for material well-being.\nD) Approval of one's own character and projects tends not to result in pleasurable feelings."]
