['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nThe first bicycle in the world was invented in 1847. Bicycles disappeared only a short time after the emergence of bicycles and did not reappear until 1860. why did this happen? A new technology will be accepted only when it is consistent with the concept of social values. So there must have been some change in social values between 1817 and 1860.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is the cause of the defect in the above reasoning?\n# Options:\nA) Ignoring the possibility that bicycles will be accepted again.\nB) This paper puts forward a question which has little to do with the conclusion of the argument.\nC) The mistaken belief that the bicycle reappeared in 1860 shows that it has been re-accepted.\nD) It is assumed that it has been truly accepted without giving a reasonable explanation.']
