proach seems to be about finding problems (through questioning) which leads to progress. Russell, on the other hand, didn\'t have this approach, so he fell behind. This also seems relevant.\n\nNow, I need to decide between B and D. The question is about what the paragraph illustrates. The paragraph talks about Wittgenstein being the best student because he asked endless questions, leading to his fame. Wittgenstein\'s success is attributed to his curiosity (B) or his ability to find problems (D).\n\nThe key point is that Wittgenstein\'s method was questioning and finding problems, which led to his success. So the paragraph is illustrating that finding problems is the premise for continuous progress, which is option D.\n\nWait, but the question is about what the paragraph is intended to illustrate. The paragraph shows that Wittgenstein\'s method (questioning) led to his success, and when asked why Russell fell behind, Wittgenstein said he had no problem, implying that Russell didn\'t find problems. So the paragraph is highlighting that finding problems is necessary for progress, which is option D.\n\nAlternatively, option B is about curiosity being the driving force, which is also true because questioning shows curiosity. But the specific point is about the method of finding problems leading to progress, which is more directly option D.\n\nSo I think the answer is D.\n'] 88%|████████▊ | 525/600 [6:04:51<19:26, 15.56s/it]
