['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nThe crux of creativity resides in the ability to manufacture variation on a theme. If we look at the history of science, for instance, we see that every idea is built upon a thousand related ideas. Careful analysis leads us to understand that what we choose to call a new theme or a new discovery is itself always and without exception some sort of variation, on a deep level, of previous themes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if all of the statements in the passage are true, each of the following must also be true EXCEPT:\n# Options:\nA) All great scientific discoverers have been able to manufacture a variation on a theme.\nB) Careful analysis of a specific variation can reveal previous themes of which it is a variation.\nC) Some new scientific discoveries do not represent, on a deep level, a variation on previous themes.\nD) No scientific idea is entirely independent of all other ideas.']
