["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nAlthough administrative decision-making in strict accordance with the scientific way of thinking can reduce mistakes and achieve accuracy, decision-making is human action after all. People do not operate according to the law and produce products on a scale as machines do.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is what this passage is intended to tell us?\n# Options:\nA) People's subjective factors can not be ignored in the process of administrative decision-making.\nB) Human subjectivity is often the main cause of decision-making mistakes.\nC) As the main body of administrative decision-making, people need to regulate their own behavior.\nD) Scientific mode of thinking is the premise of scientific administrative decision-making."]
