      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A, B, C, or D is an example of impression management based on the given definition. Let me start by understanding what impression management is. The context says it's the process where people manage their impressions of themselves to fit the current social situation or interpersonal context, ensuring others judge them favorably.\n\nSo, impression management is about how someone presents themselves in different situations to make a good impression. It's about adapting one's behavior, appearance, etc., to suit the context they're in.\n\nNow, let's look at each option one by one.\n\nOption A: The agent of a Hong Kong star has gone out of his way to increase his popularity by getting more stars to participate in TV entertainment programs. Hmm, this seems like someone is trying to boost their popularity by involving others. It's more about gaining popularity through others' actions, not necessarily managing their own impression. So maybe not A.\n\nOption B: The chairman of the board criticized manager Chen, saying that clients would not have confidence in the company if they saw such a mess in the office every day. Here, the chairman is addressing a problem in the office and making a statement about how the environment affects client confidence. It's more about addressing a problem rather than managing one's own impression. So probably not B.\n\nOption C: After hearing his classmates secretly say bad things about him, Lin couldn't help but go up and beat him. This sounds like someone reacting to negative comments by taking action. It's more about responding to others' negative remarks, not managing their own impression. So likely not C.\n\nOption D: Before the interview, in order to be hired, Xiao Li made careful preparation in clothing, hairstyle, etc. This clearly shows someone preparing their appearance and other aspects to make a good impression during an interview. It's about managing their own presentation to fit the context of the interview, aiming to make a favorable impression.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the correct answer should be D because it's about managing one's own appearance and behavior to fit the situation, which aligns with the definition of impression management.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D. \n\n**Answer:** D) Before the interview, in order to be hired, Xiao Li in the clothing, hairstyle and so on has made the careful preparation.",
