is essentially saying that protection of the family (B) can only happen if France is strong (A). So, B implies A.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) A weak France can\'t protect your family. This seems to be the contrapositive of the slogan. If France is weak, then it can\'t protect the family. But wait, the slogan is "only a strong France can protect your family," which is equivalent to "if your family is protected, then France is strong." It doesn\'t directly say that a weak France can\'t protect the family, but logically, if a strong France is necessary, then a weak France can\'t be the one doing the protecting. So A might be true.\n\nB) A strong France can protect your family. This is the converse of the slogan. The slogan says that a strong France is necessary, but it doesn\'t necessarily say that a strong France is sufficient. So, just because France is strong doesn\'t automatically mean it can protect the family. The slogan doesn\'t make a claim about the sufficiency, just the necessity. So B might not be necessarily true.\n\nC) France is weak because it does not protect the family. This seems to be the inverse of the slogan. The slogan doesn\'t claim that France is weak; it\'s making a conditional statement. So C is not supported by the slogan.\n\nD) If the family is protected, France will be strong. This is exactly what the slogan is stating. The slogan is "only a strong France can protect your family," which translates to "if the family is protected, then France is strong." So D is directly supported by the slogan.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought A might also be true because if a strong France is necessary, then a weak France can\'t protect the family. But actually, the slogan doesn\'t say that a weak France can\'t protect the family; it just says that a strong France is necessary. So A might not be the best answer because it\'s making a stronger claim than what\'s stated.\n\nSo, the correct answer should be D because it directly restates the slogan in logical terms. The slogan is an "only if" statement, which is equivalent to "if the family is protected, then France is strong." So D is the correct option.\n']
