adapted; it just says it's lagging behind now.\n\nD) Since the founding of new china, china's higher education system has undergone many changes.\nThe context does mention that higher education has changed several times since the founding, so this is true.\n\nNow, the question is which argument the paragraph mainly supports. The paragraph emphasizes that while there have been reforms and achievements, the system as a whole is still lagging behind. So, the main point is that more reform is needed to catch up.\n\nOption A directly addresses the need for further reform, which is the main point. Option B is a true statement but doesn't capture the main argument about needing more reform. Option C is too extreme and not supported by the context. Option D is a fact but not the main argument.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be A.\n</think>\n\nThe paragraph supports the argument that China's higher education system needs further reform to adapt to the ongoing economic and social developments.\n\n**Answer: A**",
