eir opposition is based on economic reasons. In option A, the beauticians\' suggestion is used to argue that people should cut their hair more often, assuming that their current behavior is beneficial. Both are using the current action or stance to justify the recommendation, rather than addressing why the current stance is wrong.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be A.\n']
