["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nSeven athletes took part in the men's 5km final: S, T, U, W, X, Y and Z. The clothes worn by athletes are either red or green, and no athletes reach the finish line at the same time. The known information is as follows: for athletes who arrive at the finish line one after another, their clothes are not all red. Y reached the finish line some time before T and W. Two of the athletes who reached the finish line before Y happened to be dressed in red. S is the sixth athlete to reach the finish line. Z arrives at the finish line at some time before U.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is listed (from left to right), which may be the ranking of athletes from the first to the seventh to reach the finish line one after another?\n# Options:\nA) X,z,u,y,w,s,t\nB) X,y,z,u,w,s,t\nC) Z,w,u,t,y,s,x\nD) Z,u,t,y,w,s,x"]
