en we encounter anything, we should keep an ordinary heart and learn to be calm.\nThis is more about maintaining calmness, but the story's main message is about not trying to catch apples that don't belong to you, not necessarily about being calm. So maybe C isn't the best choice.\n\nD) Any exploration in life is the accumulation of successful experience.\nThis suggests that every attempt leads to success, but the story actually teaches that sometimes you shouldn't try to catch something that isn't yours. So D doesn't fit.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the story emphasizes that it's okay to not catch every apple and that you shouldn't waste time on things that don't belong to you. The main message is about not being discouraged and moving on, which points to option B.\n"]
